From 8c50b268582911b069ef17a3fc6daf5509136a32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: y700-elden <research@localhost>
Date: Mon, 20 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [RFC] PCI: qcom: Skip the L2/L3 Ready LTSSM wait on SM8750

On SM8750 (which reuses the SM8550 controller IP) the LTSSM register at
PARF + 0x1b0 never reports L2_IDLE (0x15) nor a detect state (<= 0x06)
after the PME_Turn_Off broadcast.  It stays at L0S (0x12) for the whole
10 ms poll window, so every system suspend logs:

  qcom-pcie 1c00000.pcie: Timeout waiting for L2 entry! LTSSM: 0x12

This is the same class of problem pci-imx6 and pcie-ultrarisc already
work around: the controller cannot reliably read the LTSSM state after
PME_Turn_Off, so polling it is pointless.

Set pp->skip_l23_ready for this platform so dw_pcie_suspend_noirq()
follows PCIe r6.0, sec 5.3.3.2.1: broadcast PME_Turn_Off, wait 10 ms,
then continue with the L2/L3 sequence without reading LTSSM.

This patch deliberately does NOT change any power-management behaviour:
qcom_pcie_deinit_2_7_0() still gates the PCIe clocks and disables the
vdda/vddpe-3v3 regulators, and the interconnect/OPP votes in
qcom_pcie_suspend_noirq() are untouched.  The only observable change is
that the bogus warning disappears and the noirq phase is ~10 ms shorter.

Signed-off-by: y700-elden <research@localhost>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
index 8c50b26..fe15949 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -1419,6 +1419,19 @@ static int qcom_pcie_host_init(struct dw_pcie_rp *pp)
 	struct qcom_pcie *pcie = to_qcom_pcie(pci);
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * SM8750 reuses the SM8550 controller IP.  After the PME_Turn_Off
+	 * broadcast its LTSSM (PARF + 0x1b0) stays in L0S and never reaches
+	 * L2_IDLE, so polling it only produces
+	 *
+	 *   "Timeout waiting for L2 entry! LTSSM: 0x12"
+	 *
+	 * on every suspend.  Follow PCIe r6.0, sec 5.3.3.2.1 instead: send
+	 * PME_Turn_Off, wait 10 ms and continue without reading LTSSM.
+	 */
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(pci->dev->of_node, "qcom,pcie-sm8750"))
+		pp->skip_l23_ready = true;
+
 	qcom_pcie_perst_assert(pcie);
 
 	ret = pcie->cfg->ops->init(pcie);
